Subject: ALSA: usb-audio: Add jack detection for Razer Barracuda X (2022) dongle

The Razer Barracuda X (2022) 2.4 GHz dongle (1532:0552) is a UAC1 device
without jack detection, like the Sony DualSense. The out-of-tree hid-barracuda
driver in this repository reports the headset's wireless link as
SW_HEADPHONE_INSERT and SW_MICROPHONE_INSERT on a "Headset Jack" input device
parented to the same USB device. Reuse the DualSense quirk, which matches that
input device by VID:PID and parent chain, to create "Headphone Jack" and
"Headset Mic Jack" controls.

Tested on v7.2.6 with hid-barracuda 0.2.0: jacks follow headset power, and
PipeWire falls back to another output while the headset is off.
Not submitted upstream; it depends on hid-barracuda being in-tree.

diff --git a/sound/usb/mixer_quirks.c b/sound/usb/mixer_quirks.c
index 74d26fd..57b1e8e 100644
--- a/sound/usb/mixer_quirks.c
+++ b/sound/usb/mixer_quirks.c
@@ -4426,6 +4426,8 @@ int snd_usb_mixer_apply_create_quirk(struct usb_mixer_interface *mixer)
 #if IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_INPUT)
 	case USB_ID(0x054c, 0x0ce6): /* Sony DualSense controller (PS5) */
 	case USB_ID(0x054c, 0x0df2): /* Sony DualSense Edge controller (PS5) */
+	/* Link state reported by the out-of-tree hid-barracuda driver as jack switches */
+	case USB_ID(0x1532, 0x0552): /* Razer Barracuda X (2022) 2.4 GHz dongle */
 		err = snd_dualsense_controls_create(mixer);
 		break;
 #endif /* IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_INPUT) */
